// Title: Suspicious Execution of Shutdown to Log Out
// Sigma ID: ec290c06-9b6b-4338-8b6b-095c0f284f10
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-10-01 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: impact, T1529
// Description: Detects the rare use of the command line tool shutdown to logoff a user
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/9e5b12c4912c07562aec7500447b11fa3e17e254/atomics/T1529/T1529.md
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/shutdown
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_shutdown_logoff.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\shutdown.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/l"
